{
  "_what": "How a look's values degrade instead of failing (tools/screen-looks/read-data/colour-ladder.ts). A look arrives from outside: a downloaded .look.json, a Marketplace look, a value an AI wrote. When a colour is not a colour the screen can draw (a channel past its range, a hex of the wrong length, a word that names nothing), the token takes the next rung of `ladder` that is valid: `authored` is the value as given, `default` is the colour the same token has in the default look, `neutral` is the grey below. A number past its own min or max takes the nearest bound. Text that could close or escape its style rule takes the default. The look still opens and every other token stays as authored; nothing throws. Saving through save_look is stricter on purpose (screen-look-record.ts refuses a bad value with words, because the person or AI is there to fix it).",
